  "body": {
    "id": "lem:support-cleaning-algebra",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "Let \\(p,\\widehat p\\in[0,1]^K\\) satisfy \\(\\sum_i p_i=\\sum_i\\widehat p_i=1\\), let \\(0<\\tau<1/(2K)\\), and define \\(\\bar p_i=\\widehat p_i\\mathbf 1\\{\\widehat p_i>\\tau\\}/\\sum_l\\widehat p_l\\mathbf 1\\{\\widehat p_l>\\tau\\}\\).  If \\(\\delta=\\|\\widehat p-p\\|_\\infty\\), then the denominator is positive and\n\\[\n \\|\\bar p-p\\|_\\infty\\leq(2K+1)(\\delta+\\tau).\n\\]\nMoreover, if \\(p_i=0\\) and \\(\\delta\\leq\\tau\\), then \\(\\bar p_i=0\\).  Consequently, for the columnwise cleaning of \\(\\widehat M_A,\\widehat M_Z\\), on\n\\[\n \\mathcal E_{\\mathrm{clean},n}\n =\\{r_{A,\\infty}+r_{Z,\\infty}\\leq\\tau_{S,n}\\},\n\\]\nevery true-zero measurement cell is zero in \\(\\bar M_A,\\bar M_Z\\),\n\\[\n \\|\\bar M_A-M_A\\|_\\infty\\leq C_{\\mathrm{reg}}(r_{A,\\infty}+\\tau_{S,n}),\n \\qquad\n \\|\\bar M_Z-M_Z\\|_\\infty\\leq C_{\\mathrm{reg}}(r_{Z,\\infty}+\\tau_{S,n}),\n\\]\nand the corresponding conditional \\(L^2(P)\\) errors are bounded by \\(C_{\\mathrm{reg}}r_A^{\\mathrm c}\\) and \\(C_{\\mathrm{reg}}r_Z^{\\mathrm c}\\).  No lower bound on a positive coordinate of \\(p\\), \\(M_A\\), or \\(M_Z\\) is required.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "K",
      "tauS",
      "MA",
      "MZ",
      "MAbar",
      "MZbar",
      "reta",
      "Creg",
      "P"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:support-leakage-diagnostic",
      "def:quadratic-remainder"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "Put \\(t=\\sum_{l:\\,\\widehat p_l\\leq\\tau}\\widehat p_l\\).  Because \\(\\widehat p\\) is stochastic, \\(0\\leq t\\leq K\\tau<1/2\\), and the normalizing denominator is \\(1-t>0\\).  If \\(\\widehat p_i>\\tau\\), then\n\\[\n |\\bar p_i-\\widehat p_i|\n =\\widehat p_i\\frac{t}{1-t}\\leq\\frac{K\\tau}{1-K\\tau}\n \\leq2K\\tau.\n\\]\nIf \\(\\widehat p_i\\leq\\tau\\), then \\(|\\bar p_i-\\widehat p_i|=\\widehat p_i\\leq\\tau\\).  The triangle inequality therefore gives\n\\[\n \\|\\bar p-p\\|_\\infty\n \\leq\\|\\bar p-\\widehat p\\|_\\infty+\\|\\widehat p-p\\|_\\infty\n \\leq2K\\tau+\\delta\n \\leq(2K+1)(\\delta+\\tau).\n\\]\nIf \\(p_i=0\\) and \\(\\delta\\leq\\tau\\), then \\(\\widehat p_i\\leq\\tau\\), so the strict threshold makes \\(\\bar p_i=0\\).  Apply these conclusions to every column.  On \\(\\mathcal E_{\\mathrm{clean},n}\\), each of the two matrix sup-norm errors is at most \\(\\tau_{S,n}\\), and hence every true-zero entry is removed.  The displayed matrix sup-norm bounds follow from equivalence of entrywise and operator norms in the fixed dimension \\(K\\).  Finally,\n\\[\n \\|\\bar M_A-M_A\\|_{L^2(P_X)}\n \\leq \\|\\widehat M_A-M_A\\|_{L^2(P_X)}\n      +\\|\\bar M_A-\\widehat M_A\\|_{L^2(P_X)}\n \\leq r_A+2K\\tau_{S,n}\\leq C_{\\mathrm{reg}}r_A^{\\mathrm c},\n\\]\nand the same calculation applies to \\(Z\\).  The argument removes any fitted coordinate below the threshold and nowhere invokes a positive-cell lower bound.",
